            "ImageDescription": {
              "value": "Standertskjöldin talo (Standertskjöld House), built in 1885, was developed by Carl August Standertskjöld and designed by architect Theodor Höijer. This apartment building is located in the Kruununhaka neighborhood of Helsinki at Pohjoisranta 4 and Kirkkokatu 2. The street names reflect the building’s location along the northern portion of central Helsinki’s waterfront (Pohjoisranta has a meaning similar to North Quay or North Esplanade) and near major churches (Kirkkokatu means church street).",
